    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Verbs with være",
     "texto": [
      "**Have** is the most widespread auxiliary; **være** appears with certain intransitive verbs of movement or change of state: **Hun er kommet hjem.** = She has come home. The choice can also depend on the meaning: **Hun er cyklet hjem** (she cycled home), but **Hun har cyklet hele dagen** (she's been cycling all day). Learn the common uses of each verb and context."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Other verbs",
     "texto": [
      "With other verbs use **have**: **Han har løbet hele vejen.** = He has run the whole way. **Vi har læst bogen.** = We have read the book.",
      "Compare: **Han er løbet hjem.** (he's run home) and **Han har løbet hele vejen.** (he has run the whole way)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
